@@ -37,6 +37,14 @@ The clipboard is one browser-wide destination, so this plugin instance runs one
 
 When `ui-message-feedback` is mounted, the same menu also offers `Feedback`, which opens its existing Session feedback dialog. Opening or dismissing that form does not export the Session or submit feedback. The feedback row follows the feedback plugin's availability; both export actions remain available independently.
 
+### Agent Session Record export
+
+Authenticated clients can request `GET /api/session.agent-session?sessionId=<id>` to download `agent-session.jsonl`. `HEAD` performs the same session read without returning the body. The route returns 400 for invalid queries, 404 for missing sessions and a sanitized 500 for read failures.
+
+The native exporter reads a complete committed snapshot through `sessionQuery.readSession`. It preserves text, readable reasoning, system and developer instructions, tool calls, final tool results and title observations. Inherited prefixes become a gap because their original ASR record identities are unavailable. Attachments, opaque provider state, unsettled attempts, approvals and inference accounting are declared missing. No model turn runs and no session data changes. The complete JSON Lines body is buffered in memory.
+
+Backend callers can also use the pure `formatAgentSession(session, events, inheritedEventCount)` formatter. Pass the selected native header and its ordered logical events. The inherited event count excludes the shared prefix from repeated credit.
+
 ### When to choose it
 
 Choose it for a Web deployment that needs user-facing session export: a readable Markdown transcript for copying and a ZIP archive for downloading, or for a backend caller that already holds a complete committed logical event snapshot and needs the same Markdown conversion. Avoid it when a Host path write is needed: the browser operations keep their result in the browser, and the conversion utility performs no IO. The logs are serialized from persistence read handles, so any mounted backend is supported.
